# MCP server

- Endpoint: **`/mcp`** (Streamable HTTP via `mcp-handler` in `app/mcp/route.ts`).
- Tools live in `lib/mcp/tools.ts`; multi-session checklists persist in Postgres `delivery_sessions` via `lib/sessions/checklistStore.ts` (UI tabs + `/api/checklist`). Survives Railway deploys.
- Each session has a stable UUID **`id` / `sessionId`**. UI shows it on tabs; MCP write tools accept optional `sessionId` (omit = selected tab). Use `list_hauling_sessions` / `create_hauling_session` / `set_active_hauling_session`.
- Screenshot / contract intake playbook: `docs/mcp-screenshot-hauling-playbook.md` (also MCP tool `get_hauling_intake_playbook`).
- Accepted intake JSON: `hauling_contracts_intake` (`lib/missions/haulingIntake.ts`, examples in `lib/fixtures/hauling-intake/`).
- ChatGPT / Gemini / Cursor flow: `get_hauling_intake_playbook` → `store_hauling_screenshot` (attachments) → extract contracts / MobiGlas transcripts → `search_*` → optimize legs → **`apply_hauling_contracts_intake`** (with `sessionId` when needed) → `get_hauling_checklist`.
- Session ships (`shipSlugs`) come from UEX vehicle fixtures (`lib/fixtures/ships.json`); cargo SCU on those rows will drive bay capacity later.
- Cargo bay geometry for AI packing guidance: MCP tool **`get_session_cargo_grid`** (session ships or optional `ship=`). Sketches + per-ship view scale live in `lib/fixtures/cargoGrids.json` (loaded via `lib/ships/cargoGrids.ts`); placement rule summaries come from `cargoGridPlacementRules.ts`.
- Per-ship bay organization preferences: Postgres `ship_bay_preferences` (live, MCP-writable) plus committed defaults in `lib/fixtures/shipBayPreferences.json`. **Database wins** when both exist. MCP: **`list_ship_bay_preferences`**, **`get_ship_bay_preferences`**, **`update_ship_bay_preferences`** (accumulate notes/guidelines over time; does not rewrite the file). Also returned on `get_session_cargo_grid`.
- Mission catalog (planning store, not live checklist): tables `catalog_missions` / `catalog_mission_notes` / `catalog_mission_runs`; MCP **`create_mission`** (`type`, default `hauling`), `list_missions`, `get_mission`, `add_mission_note`, `record_mission_run`. Always pass **`offerLocation`** (where the offer/screenshot was seen).
- Session start point (`startLocationSlug`) is set in the UI fuzzy search or via `set_session_start_location`.
- Contract screenshots: web UI upload or MCP `store_hauling_screenshot` → `.data/mcp-screenshots/<batchId>/` (gitignored). UI uses `sessionId` as `batchId`. Retrieve with MCP `list_hauling_screenshots` / `get_hauling_screenshot`. Prefer a Railway volume on `.data` so files survive redeploy.
- When adding tools: action-oriented names, “Use this when…” descriptions, zod `inputSchema`, keep instructions on the handler updated.
- Production MCP (Railway): `https://citizen-wing-commander-production.up.railway.app/mcp` — add to Cursor via `.cursor/mcp.json` as a remote `url` server (Streamable HTTP).
- Local ChatGPT/Cursor testing can use that public HTTPS URL or a Secure MCP Tunnel pointing at `/mcp`. Do not invent locations/commodities/ships outside fixtures.
- Checklist sessions are durable in Postgres. Screenshot files live on disk under `.data/mcp-screenshots/` (mount a Railway volume at `/app/.data` in production).
